 Hi everyone,

 I'm using mlmmj for a couple of low traffic lists. Two days ago I was 
 greatly surprised to discover that mlmmj doesn't allow for people to 
 post through GMane.

 A quick scan through the archives revealed that I could use the 
 "access" feature to work around this, but I didn't understand why it was 
 needed at all. GMane does the "correct thing" by setting the envelope 
 sender to a subscribed address and faking the From: header.

 I didn't want to switch to a bigger list manager so I read through the 
 sources. In mlmmj-process there seems to be absolutely no distinction of 
 Envelope-from and From. From: is used anywhere, by restricting it to the 
 first valid From: address. Looks broken to me, especially when checking 
 for loops (comparing list-address against From).

 I patched mlmmj so that Envelope-from: is used for 
 processing/subonlypost and access control. From: is used only when 
 generating the body of help messages.

 This fixed gmane for me.

 I also shuffled mlmmj-process.c so that address validation checks are 
 performed before using the addresses themselves. listprocess.c could 
 also use some extra-cleanup (efrom is validated in 10 different places, 
 but could probably be done just once in mlmmj-process.c when efrom is 
 extracted).

 I'm attaching the patch against 1.2.17.
 Can anyone comment on this? Am I doing something wrong?
 Any chance this gets integrated?

 Thanks again.

